@andrew@codeconstruct.com.au So, I ran into a snag with your suggestion. Just having these as __attribute__(weak) did not let me override the function by defining it in https://github.com/openbmc/libpldm/blob/main/tests/transport/send_recv_timeout.cpp#L7. Probably because we build libpldm as a library and include it into the C++ test executables.

I could have send_recv_timeout.cpp define libpldm_clock_gettimeval and notice that libpldm calls its own internal function since the linter does not hold onto it.

The only way was for me to do some function pointer, expose another `libpldm_set_impl_gettimeval` which takes in a function pointer which can override internal aspects. Any ideas? Probably some linker magic?
